<div class="mt-10" id="topic-propositional-logic-definition">

    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold">
        1. Definition of Propositional Logic
    </h2>

    <div class="w-full h-[1px] flex items-center justify-center pt-[10px]">
        <div class="bg-gray-600 w-full h-[1px]"></div>
    </div>

    <p class="text-md text-gray-400 px-3 mt-3 leading-relaxed"><strong class="text-white">Propositional logic</strong> is a system of logic that studies propositions and how their truth values change when they are combined or modified. A proposition is a declarative statement that is either true or false.</p>
<div class="bg-[#1B0D2D] border border-[#3A2560] rounded-lg p-5"><h3 class="text-xl font-bold mt-6 mb-3">Examples of Propositions</h3><ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2"><li><span class="text-white">“2 + 3 = 5.”</span> — True.</li><li><span class="text-white">“10 is an odd number.”</span> — False.</li><li><span class="text-white">“Baguio is in the Philippines.”</span> — True.</li></ul></div>
<h3 class="text-xl font-bold mt-6">Statements That Are Not Propositions</h3><p class="text-md text-gray-400 px-3 mt-3 leading-relaxed">Questions, commands, and open sentences without a specified variable value do not have a definite truth value.</p>
<div class="overflow-x-auto mt-4"><table class="w-full border-collapse"><thead><tr class="border-b border-[#3A2560] text-white"><th class="p-3">Expression</th><th class="p-3">Reason</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr class="border-b border-[#3A2560]"><td class="p-3">“What time is it?”</td><td class="p-3">It is a question.</td></tr><tr class="border-b border-[#3A2560]"><td class="p-3">“Close the door.”</td><td class="p-3">It is a command.</td></tr><tr><td class="p-3">“x + 2 = 7”</td><td class="p-3">Its truth depends on the value of x.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
<p class="text-md text-gray-400 px-3 mt-3 leading-relaxed">Propositions are commonly represented by lowercase letters such as \(p\), \(q\), and \(r\). For example, let \(p\) represent “It is raining” and \(q\) represent “The ground is wet.”</p>
</div>
